{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1775376980-nnF1ytbKoN7ZdrZWBHs5","role":"assistant","created":1775377006,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have extracted the High-Grade Corporate Bond yields from all three Treasury Bulletins. Let me summarize what I found:\n\n1. **February 1943**: From the Monthly Series in 1943-03 page 68:\n   - Looking at the table: 1943-Jan shows 2.70, 1943-Feb shows 2.68\n   - February 1943 High-grade corporate bonds yield: **2.68%**\n\n2. **February 1944**: From the Monthly Series in 1944-03 page 83:\n   - Looking at the table, I can see 1944-Jan shows 2.65, and 1944-Feb shows 2.66\n   - Wait, let me look more carefully at this table.\n   \n   Actually, looking at the 1944-03 page 83:\n   - 1944-Jan: High-grade corporate = 2.65\n   - Feb: The table shows 1944-Feb in different places. Let me check again.\n   \n   Looking at the \"Monthly Series 4/ - (continued)\" section:\n   - It shows: 1944-Jan = 2.65 (from row: 1944-Jan | 1.95 | 2.49 | 2.65)\n   - Looking at the last few rows: \"Feb.\" in the 1944 section shows 2.66\n   \n   So February 1944 = **2.66%**\n\n3. **January 1945**: From the Monthly Series in 1945-03 page 71:\n   - 1945-Jan shows: 1.81 | 2.44 | 2.58\n   - January 1945 High-grade corporate bonds yield: **2.58%**\n\nNow let me calculate:\n- Benchmark: 2.60%\n\n- February 1943: |2.68 - 2.60| = 0.08\n- February 1944: |2.66 - 2.60| = 0.06\n\n\n- January 1945: |2.58 - 2.60| = 0.02\n\nI'll compute the average deviation by summing the absolute differences and dividing by 3. The result is (0.08 + 0.06 + 0.02) / 3 = 0.0533, which rounds to **0.05** percentage points.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_1a280e81aa664be3903006d5","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"write","arguments":{"path":"/app/answer.txt","content":"0.05"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
